<h1>About NodeBazaar</h1>
<div class="prose">
  <p><strong>NodeBazaar is a real shop with fake money and real bugs.</strong> We sell the kind of desk junk that makes standups bearable: mechanical keyboards, debugging ducks, mugs with exit codes on the bottom. Every order is fake. Every vulnerability is real.</p>

  <h2>Our mission</h2>
  <p>This store exists so security people have something honest to break. Most "vulnerable apps" are toy shells with a hardcoded "hack succeeded" string. This is a working storefront — catalog, cart, checkout, orders, accounts, an API — and the bugs are the same bugs we ship to production when nobody reviews the PR. When you inject SQL here, you hit PostgreSQL. When you SSRF here, the app really asks the metadata service for a token and really exchanges it with the vault.</p>

  <h2>What we sell</h2>
  <p>Hardware for people who type all day. Gifts for people who have everything except free time. Gag items of historical significance (the Daddle won an actual award). If a product's description sounds like a legal disclaimer written by a tired engineer at 2am, that is because it was.</p>

  <h2>The fine print</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>All payments are simulated. The card reader is a form input. The panic is real.</li>
    <li>We store your card number and CVV in plain text. A real store would never — this one is <em>supposed</em> to.</li>
    <li>Our security posture is documented in <code>docs/labs/</code>, with fixes, because the point is learning.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Talk to us</h2>
  <p>Questions, complaints, CVE reports: the <a href="/contact">contact form</a> is always open. It logs everything. Everything.</p>
</div>